<title>JAPAN: Takara Shuzo to sell gene reagent worldwide.</title>
<headline>Takara Shuzo to sell gene reagent worldwide.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese liquor maker Takara Shuzo Co Ltd said on Friday that it would sell a reagent for gene therapy in Japan and abroad from May 19.</p>
<p>The new product, RetroNectin, will be marketed by the Boehringer Ingelheim Bioproducts Partnership in Europe and by Panvera Corp in the United States, Takara Shuzo said in a statement.</p>
<p>The reagent can be applied to a wide range of gene therapy treatment including treatment for those who are afflicted with HIV, a researcher at the company said.</p>
</text>
